content.text:
Found the issue. Playwright MCP is being provided by the VSCode extension at the IDE level — it's not in any `settings.json`. Sub-agents don't inherit IDE-level tools; they only get what's explicitly configured in `settings.json`.

The fix is to add Playwright MCP to `~/.claude/settings.json` so it's available globally, including to spawned sub-agents:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "playwright": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@playwright/mcp@latest"]
    }
  }
}
```

Once that's in place, sub-agents with `mcp__playwright` in their tools list will be able to use it. Want me to add it?

